### Step 2: Apply the shoelace formula
The shoelace formula for the area \( \mathcal{A} \) is:

\[
\mathcal{A} = \frac{1}{2} \left| \sum_{\text{forward}} (x_i y_{i+1}) - \sum_{\text{backward}} (y_i x_{i+1}) \right|
