To find the values of \( k \) and \( b \) that minimize the expression \(\sum_{i=1}^{4} |y_i - (kx_i + b)|^2\), we need to find the least squares solution for the linear regression problem. This involves minimizing the sum of the squared residuals.

Given the points \((0,0)\), \((1,8)\), \((3,8)\), and \((4,20)\), we can set up the following matrix equation to find \( k \) and \( b \):

\[
X = \begin{bmatrix}
1 & 0 \\
1 & 1 \\
1 & 3 \\
1 & 4
\end{bmatrix}, \quad
y = \begin{bmatrix}
0 \\
8 \\
8 \\
20
\end{bmatrix}, \quad
\vec{\theta} = \begin{bmatrix}
b \\
k
\end{bmatrix}
\]

The least squares solution is given by:

\[
\vec{\theta} = (X^T X)^{-1} X^T y
\]

First, compute \( X^T X \):

\[
X^T X = \begin{bmatrix}
1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\
0 & 1 & 3 & 4
\end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix}
1 & 0 \\
1 & 1 \\
1 & 3 \\
1 & 4
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
4 & 8 \\
8 & 26
\end{bmatrix}
\]

Next, compute the inverse of \( X^T X \):

\[
(X^T X)^{-1} = \frac{1}{4 \cdot 26 - 8 \cdot 8} \begin{bmatrix}
26 & -8 \\
-8 & 4
\end{bmatrix}
= \frac{1}{104 - 64} \begin{bmatrix}
26 & -8 \\
-8 & 4
\end{bmatrix}
= \frac{1}{40} \begin{bmatrix}
26 & -8 \\
-8 & 4
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
\frac{26}{40} & \frac{-8}{40} \\
\frac{-8}{40} & \frac{4}{40}
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
\frac{13}{20} & \frac{-1}{5} \\
\frac{-1}{5} & \frac{1}{10}
\end{bmatrix}
\]

Now, compute \( X^T y \):

\[
X^T y = \begin{bmatrix}
1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\
0 & 1 & 3 & 4
\end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix}
0 \\
8 \\
8 \\
20
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
1 \cdot 0 + 1 \cdot 8 + 1 \cdot 8 + 1 \cdot 20 \\
0 \cdot 0 + 1 \cdot 8 + 3 \cdot 8 + 4 \cdot 20
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
36 \\
120
\end{bmatrix}
\]

Finally, compute \( \vec{\theta} \):

\[
\vec{\theta} = (X^T X)^{-1} X^T y = \begin{bmatrix}
\frac{13}{20} & \frac{-1}{5} \\
\frac{-1}{5} & \frac{1}{10}
\end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix}
36 \\
120
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
\frac{13}{20} \cdot 36 + \frac{-1}{5} \cdot 120 \\
\frac{-1}{5} \cdot 36 + \frac{1}{10} \cdot 120
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
\frac{468}{20} - \frac{120}{5} \\
- \frac{36}{5} + \frac{120}{10}
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
23.4 - 24 \\
-7.2 + 12
\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}
-0.6 \\
4.8
\end{bmatrix}
\]

So, the values are \( b = -0.6 \) and \( k = 4.8 \).

The integer part of \( k \) is:

\[
